Subject: [PATCH 118/118] feat(refinery): add merge-push.sh and prove it
 matches the formula lane (gcp-l8td.5)

B1 phase 3, step 2 (gcp-l8td.3 DESIGN, Sequencing 2). The refinery runs
mol-refinery-patrol's merge-push step as 14 fenced blocks stitched and
hand-rendered in the agent's shell on every patrol, about 30% of its tool
calls. gastown/assets/scripts/refinery/merge-push.sh runs the same lane
(direct, mr, local) as one process with resolved config. It is additive:
the formula does not call it yet and is byte-identical. B1.2b (gcp-l8td.6)
switches over.

How the script was built. Every helper and lane block was taken through
tomllib, the renderer's own un-escape (so \\1 is \1), never copied out of
the .toml bytes, and only the edits the bead allows were applied, each
asserted by exact match count: template vars become resolved CFG_* values;
every gh call site, command -v included, goes through "$GH"
(REFINERY_GH, or --gh); every drain-ack/exit becomes the design's status
return (8 halt_false_completion, 9 block_existing_pr without the
pour/assign/burn, 11 local, 2 for every hard stop, merge_ff_push's own
statuses passed through); the approval gate is the canonicalized sibling
../checks/merge-approval-gate.sh with no gc formula list lookup; and the
lane glue the prose described is lane_direct, lane_mr and lane_local,
dispatched by main after the strategy promotions. The rendered text keeps
two harmless tomllib artifacts verbatim: \n inside single-quoted printf/tr
arguments renders as a literal newline, and backslash-continued lines are
joined. Both execute exactly as the formula does today.

New code around the moved text: resolve_config (flag > the rig's
FormulaVars from `gc config show --json` or MERGE_PUSH_CONFIG_JSON > derived
> embedded default; a present-but-empty key wins; an unreadable config or
missing rig entry resolves require_merge_approval ON and says so), a
`merge-push: LANE` line, a final `merge-push: RESULT <status> <summary>`
line, and MERGE_PUSH_SOURCE_ONLY=1. Two stop sites that were prose-only
now have code: a failed --force-with-lease push (2) and a verified PR with
no URL or number (2). A landed merge whose bead close fails returns 2 with
no cleanup, so origin/$BRANCH survives for the next patrol's merge-state
gate to close it as already merged. Cleanups never change the status; mr
cleanup is still today's `git checkout "$TARGET"` (B1.2b fixes it).

test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh gains a script adapter. The 23 lane cases
run once per adapter with identical assertions, and the suite fails unless
both passes count 23. The script adapter maps run_lane's var overrides into
a FormulaVars fixture and applies the design's status table through the
same gc stub (a stand-in for B1.2b's step table). One harness correction,
for both adapters: the formula adapter now renders binding_prefix=gastown.,
the value the patrol pours with for testrig/gastown.refinery, so the
false-completion witness is testrig/gastown.witness. Script-only cases pin
the invariants (executable, no {{, no drain-ack, no pour/burn), config
precedence, binding_prefix derivation, the fail-closed gate on an
unreadable config (lane mr, status 4, APPROVAL GATE REFUSED), the embedded
defaults against [vars.*].default, and REFINERY_GH reaching the PR calls.

Validation: the suite prints formula: 23 cases and script: 23 cases and
passes. Changing the mayor nudge in a scratch copy's halt_false_completion
and pointing SCRIPT at it fails script:direct_false_completion_halts and
script:mr_zero_diff_halts, while the formula pass stays green.

